k\narea and along highway 160 to Wolf Creek Pass.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T11:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.03011cf1c8199da5de650405af1eee2a145ac204.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.03011cf1c8199da5de650405af1eee2a145ac204.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 9:43PM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Ample sub-tropical moisture will bring periods of moderate to\nheavy rain across the area from tonight into Friday morning\nbefore winding down Friday afternoon.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.07b206f85aa13647288ef4fe258fb417ba10c3ce.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.07b206f85aa13647288ef4fe258fb417ba10c3ce.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 6:41PM MDT until October 23 at 3:45AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall is\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Southern Mineral County in south central Colorado...\nWestern Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 345 AM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Rock falls are\noccuring in the steeper terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 639 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain. Flooding is already occurring in the warned area.\nBetween 1 and 3.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 2 inches are possible in the\nwarned area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nWolf Creek Pass and the creeks and streams flowing into the San\nJuan River.\n- Highway 160 over Wolf Creek Pass is closed due to flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T03:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5289a6353d07b40dfaad5f421c3d49793e9f3d0c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5289a6353d07b40dfaad5f421c3d49793e9f3d0c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T05:28:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 230528 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1128 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flood Watch remains through the day Friday for the eastern San Juan mountains and the Upper Rio Grande Valley, with areal stream/river flooding and rock/mud slides possible. - Periods of moderate to heavy rain for the Continental Divide, tonight into early Friday","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-22T06:48:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 220648 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1248 AM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-231300- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},